# Build context exclusions for builds that use the repository root as context.
#
# Only the web image does (see web/Dockerfile): it needs `api/oss/*.schema.json`
# alongside `web/`, so its context cannot be `./web`. The api, ble, log and mdns
# images each use their own subdirectory as context and therefore read their own
# .dockerignore, not this file.
#
# Without this, the root context is ~1.2 GB and every build ships node_modules,
# the venv and the git history to the daemon.

.git
.venv
.venv-*
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output and caches
dist
**/dist
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
coverage
**/coverage
.ruff_cache

# Local data and logs
*.sqlite*
log/*.log

# Everything the web build has no use for. Listed rather than inverted with an
# allow-list so a new top-level directory is included by default — a missing file
# fails the build loudly, whereas a silently excluded one is what broke this in
# the first place.
docker-compose*.yaml
